{"uta": [{"id": "uta", "headword": "उत", "headword_slp1": "uta", "fold": "uta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत (I) a. (f. ता) Woven.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "उत (II) ind. A particle expressing- (1) doubt, indecision (or), तत्किमयतमातपदोषः स्यादुत यथा मे मनसि वर्तते Sak.iii., पिबामः शास्त्रौधानुत विविधकाव्यामृतरसान् Bhartr.iii.40; (2) alternative, option (or), K.S.vi.23 (in these two senses it is usually a correlative of किम् meaning ‘whether’); (3) connection, association (and, also), अधर्मोऽभिभवत्युत Bg.ii.29; (4) interrogation. (Sometimes it is used as a mere expletive).With आहो or आहोस्वित् or स्वित्, it is used as a particle of doubt or deliberation, e.g. यक्षी वा राक्षसी वा त्वमुताहोऽसि सुरांगना.With किम्, it expresses- (1) ‘or,’ किमुत सकले जाते वाह्निप्रैयत्वामिहेष्यसि Am.S.9; (2) ‘how much more,’ ‘how much less’ चेतो मुनेरपि हरेत्किमुतास्मदीयम् Ch.P.39, or मयि नांतकोऽपि प्रभुः प्रहर्तुं किमुतान्याहिंस्राः R.ii.62.With प्रति, it means ‘on the contrary,’ सामवादाः सकोपस्य तस्य प्रत्युत दीपकाः Sis.ii.55.When repeated, it has the sense of ‘either-or.’", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उतं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["utaM"]}, {"id": "utA", "headword": "उता", "headword_slp1": "utA", "fold": "uta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत (I) a. (f. ता) Woven.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "utta", "headword": "उत्त", "headword_slp1": "utta", "fold": "uta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्त a. (f. त्ता) Wet, moist.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उत्तं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["uttaM"]}, {"id": "uttA", "headword": "उत्ता", "headword_slp1": "uttA", "fold": "uta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्त a. (f. त्ता) Wet, moist.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "utaTya": [{"id": "utaTya", "headword": "उतथ्य", "headword_slp1": "utaTya", "fold": "utaTya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उतथ्य m. The name of a son of Angiras.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उतथ्यः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["utaTyaH"]}], "utaTyanuja": [{"id": "utaTyAnuja", "headword": "उतथ्यानुज", "headword_slp1": "utaTyAnuja", "fold": "utaTyanuja", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उतथ्य-अनुज, -अनुजन्मन् m. Bṛhaspati, the teacher of gods, तथ्यामुतथ्यानुजवज्जगादाग्रे गदाग्रजम् Sis.ii.69.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उतथ्यानुजः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["utaTyAnujaH"]}], "utaTyanujanman": [{"id": "utaTyAnujanman", "headword": "उतथ्यानुजन्मन्", "headword_slp1": "utaTyAnujanman", "fold": "utaTyanujanman", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उतथ्य-अनुज, -अनुजन्मन् m. Bṛhaspati, the teacher of gods, तथ्यामुतथ्यानुजवज्जगादाग्रे गदाग्रजम् Sis.ii.69.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "utansa": [{"id": "uttaMsa", "headword": "उत्तंस", "headword_slp1": "uttaMsa", "fold": "utansa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तंस m.n. 1. An ear-ring, Bh.V.ii.55; 2. a crest, an ornament worn on the crown of the head. (Note. When preceded by the word कर्ण, उत्तंस loses part of its original meaning and expresses merely ‘an ornament’ according to some. According to Mammata, the word कर्ण expresses in such cases कर्ण स्थितत्व, this, however, being merely a device to explain away the usage of standard authors, कर्णावतंसादिपदे कर्णादिध्वनिनिर्मितिः । संनिधानादिबोधार्थं स्थितेष्वेतत्समर्थनम् K.Pr.vii.).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उत्तंसः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["uttaMsaH"]}], "utawa": [{"id": "uttawa", "headword": "उत्तट", "headword_slp1": "uttawa", "fold": "utawa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तट a. (f. टा) Overflowing its banks, R.xi.58.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "uttawA", "headword": "उत्तटा", "headword_slp1": "uttawA", "fold": "utawa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तट a. (f. टा) Overflowing its banks, R.xi.58.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "utapta": [{"id": "uttapta", "headword": "उत्तप्त", "headword_slp1": "uttapta", "fold": "utapta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तप्त n. Dried flesh.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उत्तप्तं", "उत्तप्तः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["uttaptaM", "uttaptaH"]}], "utama": [{"id": "uttama", "headword": "उत्तम", "headword_slp1": "uttama", "fold": "utama", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तम (I) a. (f. मा) 1. Uppermost, highest; 2. most elevated, principal; 3. best, excellent, प्रायेणाधममध्यमो तमगुणः संवासतो जायते Bhartr.ii.67, Bg.i.24; 4. first, greatest, M.ii.249.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "उत्तम (II) m. 1. Viṣṇu; 2. the last person equivalent to the first person in English grammar (in gram.)", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उत्तमः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["uttamaH"]}, {"id": "uttamA", "headword": "उत्तमा", "headword_slp1": "uttamA", "fold": "utama", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तम (I) a. (f. मा) 1. Uppermost, highest; 2. most elevated, principal; 3. best, excellent, प्रायेणाधममध्यमो तमगुणः संवासतो जायते Bhartr.ii.67, Bg.i.24; 4. first, greatest, M.ii.249.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "उत्तमा f. An excellent woman.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "utamanga": [{"id": "uttamAMga", "headword": "उत्तमांग", "headword_slp1": "uttamAMga", "fold": "utamanga", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तम-अंग n. the head, कश्चिद्विषत्खड्गहृतो तमांगः R.vii.51, K.S.vii.41, Ve.iii., Bg.xi.27.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["उत्तमाङ्ग", "उत्तमाङ्गं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["uttamANga", "uttamANgaM"]}], "utamaDama": [{"id": "uttamADama", "headword": "उत्तमाधम", "headword_slp1": "uttamADama", "fold": "utamaDama", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "उत्तम-अधम a. high and low.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "uta